# Server behaviour for pawel.rosol.pl on mydevil.net.
#
# mydevil serves PHP-type sites through nginx with an in-house .htaccess
# module, so only the directives its documentation lists are safe here:
# https://pomoc.mydevil.net/htaccess/
# A syntax error in this file returns 500 for the whole site. To roll back,
# delete it and redeploy.
#
# Jekyll skips dotfiles, so this file is deployed only because `include:` in
# _config.yml names it.

# --- Force HTTPS -----------------------------------------------------------
# Plain HTTP used to answer 200, which left every page reachable unencrypted
# and duplicated. The ACME exception keeps Let's Encrypt renewals working over
# HTTP, which is where the http-01 challenge is fetched.
RewriteEngine On
RewriteCond %{HTTPS} off
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !^/\.well-known/acme-challenge/
RewriteRule (.*) https://%{HTTP_HOST}%{REQUEST_URI} [R=301,L]

# --- Character encoding ----------------------------------------------------
# llms.txt and security.txt are served as text/plain with no charset, which
# mangles Polish diacritics. HTML carries its own meta charset and is
# unaffected.
AddDefaultCharset utf-8

# --- Security headers ------------------------------------------------------
# No Content-Security-Policy yet: the site still loads fonts and scripts from
# googleapis, gstatic and jsdelivr. CSP comes after the assets/lib submodule
# is initialised and assets.self_host is switched on.
Header set Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
Header set X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
Header set Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
Header set X-Frame-Options "SAMEORIGIN"
Header set Permissions-Policy "geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()"

# --- Directory listings ----------------------------------------------------
Options -Indexes
